<title>FINLAND: Metra jumps on news of diesel unit merger.</title>
<headline>Metra jumps on news of diesel unit merger.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1996-09-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Finnish engineering group Metra Oy Ab rose in brisk trade on Thursday on news of a planned merger between its Wartsila diesel unit and Italian Fincantieri's diesel engine operations, brokers said.</p>
<p>At 1630/1330 GMT, Metra B traded at two-year high 248.00 markka, up nine markka or 3.77 percent. Metra's less liquid A shares were up 11.00 markka at 247.00. The aggregate volume was heavy for Metra at around 25 million markka.</p>
<p>&quot;Once the market digested the news of the merger, it was time to rush out and buy the share,&quot; one broker said.</p>
<p>-- Helsinki newsroom + 358 - 0 - 680 50 240</p>
</text>
